<%#
  A DEGRADATION IS NOT A FAILURE AND IS NOT SILENT EITHER (INV-4).

  --- WHY THIS IS A PARTIAL, AND WHY IT IS RENDERED UNCONDITIONALLY ---

  It used to be six lines inside `preview.html.erb`, nested inside the branch that only
  runs when the PDF SUCCEEDED — so a degradation recorded by a Liquid tag, on a render
  with no engine or a failed one, reached nobody. `show.html.erb` printed none at all.
  An independent review measured the consequence for T-31's new refusal: the author got
  `TOTAL=[0]` with no explanation on either page.

  So it lives in one place, both pages render it, and neither wraps it in a condition
  about something else. wkhtmltopdf stamps `legacy_engine` on every render by design; an
  unresolved asset is a real hole in the document; a refused aggregation source is a
  report that could not be computed. All are printed, because the author is the only
  person who can decide which of the three they are looking at.
%>
<% if outcome && outcome.degradations.any? %>
  <div class="reporter-degradations">
    <p><strong><%= l(:label_reporter_preview_degradations) %></strong></p>
    <ul>
      <%# `reporter_degradation_text` and not `to_s`: a code with a locale key becomes a
          sentence in the reader's language, and one without still prints its raw `to_s` so
          nothing disappears. See the helper for which codes are covered and why the rest
          are §Findings S-17 rather than this partial's problem. %>
      <% outcome.degradations.each do |degradation| %>
        <li><%= reporter_degradation_text(degradation) %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </div>
<% end %>
